# ==============================================================================
# 🪙 Soma Token ($SOMA) - Environment Configuration (.env.example)
# ==============================================================================
# This file is an example template. Duplicate this file as '.env' for live deployments.
# '.env' is excluded by .gitignore to keep your private keys safe and secret.
# ==============================================================================

# 1. Your 24-word Testnet/Mainnet wallet mnemonic (seed phrase)
# Separate each word with a single space.
WALLET_MNEMONIC="word1 word2 word3 word4 word5 word6 word7 word8 word9 word10 word11 word12 word13 word14 word15 word16 word17 word18 word19 word20 word21 word22 word23 word24"

# 2. Wallet version (Tonkeeper standard is v4 or v5r1)
WALLET_VERSION="v5r1"

# 3. Public GitHub Raw or IPFS URL of your token metadata.json
METADATA_URI="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/bnbxeth/soma-token/main/metadata.json"

# 4. (Optional) Custom Admin Address
# Leave blank to automatically use your connected deployer wallet as Admin.
ADMIN_ADDRESS=""

# ==============================================================================
# 🛠️ CLI Commands Cheat Sheet
# ==============================================================================
# Open your terminal, navigate to 'cd contracts', and run the commands as needed:
#
# 1. Deploy Soma Token ($SOMA) to Testnet:
#    npx blueprint run deploySomaToken --testnet --mnemonic
#    (Deploys the Jetton Minter contract and sets your wallet as the Owner/Admin)
#
# 2. Mint 100M or 200M Fixed Supply in 1-click:
#    npx blueprint run mintInitialSupply --testnet --mnemonic
#    (Presents an interactive menu to mint initial token supply to your wallet)
#
# 3. Quick Mint any custom amount to any address:
#    npx blueprint run quickMint --testnet --mnemonic
#    (Mints a specific token quantity to your wallet or a user's wallet)
#
# 4. Deploy Soma Treasury (Vault) Contract:
#    npx blueprint run deploySomaTreasury --testnet --mnemonic
#    (Deploys the on-chain vault that collects user verification fees)
#
# 5. Check Vault Balance & Sweep/Withdraw TON:
#    npx blueprint run treasuryController --testnet --mnemonic
#    (Allows only the Admin to sweep/withdraw all collected TON to personal wallet)
#
# 6. Run Automated Unit Tests (Free, Zero Gas):
#    npx blueprint test SomaToken.spec.ts SomaTreasury.spec.ts
#    (Executes local sandbox simulation tests; 12/12 passing)
#
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 💡 Connection Modes:
# * '--mnemonic': Signs and executes transactions locally from .env instantly.
# * '--tonconnect': Generates a QR code to approve transactions via mobile Tonkeeper.
# ==============================================================================
